    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "The club has 10 members, 5 boys and 5 girls. To find the probability that the two chosen members are both girls, we need to find the number of ways to choose 2 girls out of the 5 available girls and divide it by the total number of ways to choose any 2 members out of the 10.\n\nNumber of ways to choose 2 girls out of 5: $\\binom{5}{2} = \\frac{5!}{2!(5-2)!} = \\frac{5 \\times 4}{2 \\times 1} = 10$\n\nNumber of ways to choose any 2 members out of 10: $\\binom{10}{2} = \\frac{10!}{2!(10-2)!} = \\frac{10 \\times 9}{2 \\times 1} = 45$\n\nProbability that the two chosen members are both girls: $\\frac{\\text{Number of ways to choose 2 girls}}{\\text{Total number of ways to choose any 2 members}} = \\frac{10}{45} = \\boxed{\\frac{2}{9}}$\n\nSo, the probability that the two chosen members are both girls is $\\boxed{\\frac{2}{9}}$.",
